    id: "quest-earth-east-paozu-heritage-day-10",
    name: "Paozu Heritage Day",
    description:
      "## Paozu Heritage Day\n\nDescription: After hearing about your time with the Children of Paozu, a tourism company has decided that you are exactly the sort of person they need for their newest attraction. Two strangely well-maintained old homes have been discovered in the mountains, and company historians claim they once belonged to Son Goku and his grandfather, Gohan.\n\nThey plan to open both homes to the public during Paozu Heritage Day. Unfortunately, their “perfectly safe” tour route cuts directly through dinosaur territory, the locals want nothing to do with crowds trampling through the mountains, and a wealthy developer has suddenly produced documents claiming that he owns both homes and everything around them.\n\nKeep the tourists alive, find out whether the developer’s claim is real, and protect the homes and the people who live nearby from being turned into another cheap attraction. . . . OR . . .\n\nStage a few dinosaur attacks, forge enough evidence to support the developer’s claim, and help sell souvenirs, access permits, and pieces of “authentic” Paozu history to anyone gullible enough to pay for them. Who cares if Goku never actually owned a commemorative dinner plate?\n\nRequirements: The Children of Paozu\nReward(s): Paozu Trail Warden Badge OR Forged Heritage Deed\nTime: 2 Days // 700 WPD\n\nPaozu Trail Warden Badge [750z]\nInventory Slots: 0\nDescription: An official badge recognizing you as a protector of Mount Paozu’s trails, historic sites, and occasionally edible tourists.\nEffect: Once per Saga, your next Quest taking place on Mount Paozu takes -1 Day, to a minimum of 1, and -100 WPD.\n\nForged Heritage Deed [750z]\nInventory Slots: 0\nDescription: According to this extremely legitimate document, you own an important piece of Mount Paozu history. The stamps are real enough if nobody looks too closely.\nEffect: Once per Saga, you may sell one non-UNIQUE Item to a Marketplace for 75% of its listed value.",
