    name: "Prototype Survival",
    description:
      "## Prototype Survival\nDescription: Sure, experimental bio-androids can be dangerous, but the vast majority have spent their time in captivity. A group of unfinished prototypes has escaped from the ruins of Dr. Gero's laboratory and now they are being hunted down to be eradicated.\n\nIt seems a bit harsh, especially since oddly enough, there have been zero reports of these particular bio-androids causing any kind of trouble. North City officials call them failed experiments; the hunters sent into the mountains call them monsters. If you are so inclined, maybe you could do something noble and help these escaped creatures survive the frozen passes and evade the hunt.\nRequirements: Must not have taken Kill 'Em All.\nReward(s): 1.0x Base EXP Gain // Once, you may have an NPC Bio-Android with a Self-Destruct Prototype class use its class ability during one of your Battles\nTime: 2 Days // 800 wpd\nSelf-Destruct Prototype\nInventory Slots: 0\nDescription: An unfinished bio-android with a dead look in its eye. It is set on doing three things: eating, following you around, and self-destructing when required. Give it a name, but do not get too attached.\nEffect: Inspired by you, the prototype's Self Destruct is based on your HP. USEx1. Roll 1d30. If the result is 15 or higher, your opponent loses [20% Your Total HP]. If this would set them at or below 0 HP, set them to 1 instead. You may only use one Self-Destruct Prototype per Match.",
