    id: "quest-earth-north-smuggler-s-whiteout-13",
    name: "Smuggler’s Whiteout",
    description:
      "## Smuggler’s Whiteout\n\nDescription: A blizzard has swallowed the roads leading out of North City, which makes it the perfect night to move something that nobody is supposed to see. A convoy of smugglers is carrying technology recovered from the ruins of Dr. Gero’s laboratory, and several interested parties want to make sure it reaches its destination.\n\nEscort the convoy through the storm, protect the cargo from North City officials, and make sure the smugglers keep their end of the deal. . . . OR . . .\n\nTrack the convoy, steal the technology, or turn the whole operation over to North City. Between the smugglers, the police, and the buyers waiting at the other end, somebody is bound to pay you.\n\nRequirements: None\nReward(s): Gero Evidence Drive OR Gero Override Chip\nTime: 3 Days // 700 WPD\n\nGero Evidence Drive [1,000z]\nInventory Slots: 0\nDescription: A damaged data drive containing records from one of Dr. Gero’s abandoned projects. Most of it is encrypted, but what remains is enough to open a few doors.\nEffect: Once per Saga, your next Quest involving Dr. Gero, the Red Ribbon Army, or one of their facilities takes -1 Day, to a minimum of 1. If that Quest contains a Quest Battle, you begin the Battle with +1 KI Point.\n\nGero Override Chip [1,000z]\nInventory Slots: 1\nDescription: A small control chip designed to interrupt and override other machines. It probably will not become self-aware. Probably.\nEffect: USEx1. Activate when an opponent uses a Technology Item. NEGATE that Item’s effect.",
