    name: "How to Kill a Mockingbird",
    description:
      "## How to Kill a Mockingbird\r\nDescription: Central Command of District 8 has a thorn in its side, and they want that thorn nuked back into the stone age. That thorn happens to be Icarrus Carr: talking bird, thief, and smuggler of developing technologies. Icarrus has been spotted at a gas station eating ringdings and eyeing the monolithic Valor Corp™ R&D Facility nearby, and Central Command is waiting for him. By this point, however, they suspect a mole is aiding him.\r\nSo they've hired you to protect their findings and stop the thief before he can rob them for the third time this year .... or so that you can be the mole for Icarrus and his heist gang.\r\nRequirements: None\r\nReward(s): 400z // Once this Saga you may have a quest cost -1 Day and 1/2 WPD, before any other reductions.\r\nAlternate Reward(s): 800z ... OR ... One Technology Item worth 1,300z or less.\r\nTime: 3 Days // 700 WPD\r\n\r\nCapsule Corps: Going Green!\r\nDescription: Ever since their collaboration with Earth, many of the weaker-caste Namekians have taken a renewed interest in engineering. While they may not be the friendliest with Earth anymore, their friendship with Capsule Corps. is alive and well.\r\nWith funding and assistance from Capsule Corps., the Namekians have begun to make their own tech teams! Unlike on Earth, however, these engineering teams do not have companies, and instead work for the good of their village. They’re a bit short on staff right now and could use somebody who can handle heavy lifting. They may have er...lost a shipment or two in the sea connecting their islands. Give them a hand and they may just whip something up for you!\r\nRequirements: None\r\nRewards: 1 Technology item of 1,500z value or less.\r\nTime: 2 Days // 600 WPD",
